1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,740
In 1920,

2
00:00:01,740 --> 00:00:02,720
one man promised

3
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:03,700
to grow your money

4
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:04,820
by 50%

5
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:06,767
in 45 days.

6
00:00:06,787 --> 00:00:07,947
Charles Ponzi said

7
00:00:07,947 --> 00:00:08,567
he was trading

8
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:11,120
international postal coupons.

9
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:12,398
He wasn't.

10
00:00:12,418 --> 00:00:13,698
He paid early investors

11
00:00:13,698 --> 00:00:14,718
with money from

12
00:00:14,718 --> 00:00:15,598
new ones,

13
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:15,998
and the crowds

14
00:00:15,998 --> 00:00:17,373
kept coming.

15
00:00:17,393 --> 00:00:18,793
When reporters checked,

16
00:00:18,793 --> 00:00:19,613
there weren't enough coupons

17
00:00:19,613 --> 00:00:20,493
in the world

18
00:00:20,493 --> 00:00:21,613
to cover it.

19
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:22,333
The scheme collapsed

20
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:23,053
in August,

21
00:00:23,053 --> 00:00:24,153
and it still carries

22
00:00:24,153 --> 00:00:25,037
his name.
